Third-party software. Nollie runs Hermes Agent by Nous Research (MIT), which it downloads at a pinned
version; the Hermes files Nollie's runtime overlays keep Hermes's license, in
Services/Runtime/HermesOverlay/LICENSE-hermes-agent.txt. Nollie Computer is built from Cua Driver (MIT); its
notices are in Tools/computer-helper/NOTICE.txt. Further notices follow.

Nollie installs Cua's Hermes plugin (hermes-cua-spaces, https://github.com/trycua/hermes-cua-spaces,
pinned to commit fcf30603cfe1cc8dca61582cddc9b66f1b018134) into a helper's Hermes when the person turns
on "A computer of its own". It is used unmodified under the MIT License:

